file floppy.img

floppy.img: DOS/MBR boot sector, OEM-ID "mkfs.fat", sectors 2880, FAT (12 bit)

The image is a standard 1.44 MB FAT12 floppy disk image formatted with mkfs.fat.

Using The Sleuth Kit (fls), we listed the filesystem entries, including unallocated/deleted ones:

Bash
fls -r -p -a floppy.img

Step 3: File Carving (Data Recovery)
Extracting the raw inode directly using icat produced an incomplete PDF file (the initial cover text asking "Sei riuscito a sottrarre un floppy disk..."), as the FAT metadata pointers were unlinked or zeroed out.

To recover the complete underlying PDF stream from unallocated sectors, we performed raw file carving using Foremost:

Bash
foremost -t pdf -i floppy.img -o output_pdf/

pdftotext output_pdf/pdf/00000034.pdf -
